1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,430
You've done hundreds of curls. And your
arms still look the same.

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,050
It's not your genetics.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,590
It's the exercises.

4
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:12,790
Today, I'll show you the two exercises
that actually build big arms.

5
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:15,120
And why most guys never do them.

6
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:20,490
Stay until the end, because there's also a
bonus muscle that almost nobody trains.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,380
But first, you need to understand one
thing.

8
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:26,880
Your biceps is not the biggest muscle in
your arm.

9
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:28,220
It's your triceps.

10
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:31,750
Your triceps makes up about two thirds of
your upper arm.

11
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,810
So if you only do curls, you're ignoring
most of your arm.

12
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:40,850
That's why so many skinny guys have small
arms, even after months of training.

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,040
They train the small muscle, and forget
the big one.

14
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:45,570
And there's a second problem.

15
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,610
Most people train their arms in the wrong
position.

16
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,110
Here's what science found.

17
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:53,980
A muscle grows more when you train it in a
stretched position.

18
00:00:54,130 --> 00:01:02,460
In one study, people who trained their
triceps with their arms overhead grew
about forty percent more than people who
did normal pushdowns.

19
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:05,780
Same muscle. Same effort. Way more growth.

20
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:07,570
Just because of the position.

21
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:09,230
So the secret is simple.

22
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,790
Stretch the muscle, then make it work.

23
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,630
And that brings us to exercise number one.

24
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,990
The overhead triceps extension.

25
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:20,180
Hold one dumbbell with both hands, above
your head.

26
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:22,790
Keep your elbows close, pointing forward.

27
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:27,550
Slowly lower the weight behind your head,
until you feel a deep stretch.

28
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:30,550
Then push it back up, and squeeze at the
top.

29
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:34,170
This puts the long head of your triceps in
a full stretch.

30
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:37,320
And the long head is the biggest part of
the triceps.

31
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,640
This is the part that makes your arm look
thick from the side.

32
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:42,000
No dumbbell at home?

33
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:45,080
Use a backpack filled with books, or a
water bottle.

34
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:47,250
Same movement, same stretch.

35
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,950
Exercise number two.

36
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,900
The incline dumbbell curl.

37
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:55,870
Sit on a bench tilted back, and let your
arms hang straight down behind your body.

38
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:59,180
Now your biceps is stretched before you
even start.

39
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:02,420
Curl the weights up slowly, without moving
your elbows.

40
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:06,570
Then lower them all the way down, until
your arms are completely straight.

41
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,980
This hits the long head of your biceps.

42
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:11,130
That's the part that creates the peak.

43
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,720
The ball on top of your arm when you flex.

44
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:14,930
No bench at home?

45
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:17,330
Do chin-ups with your palms facing you.

46
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:21,340
Hang all the way down at the bottom, then
pull your chest to the bar.

47
00:02:21,490 --> 00:02:25,980
It's one of the best biceps builders in
the world, and you only need a bar.

48
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:27,740
And now, the bonus.

49
00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:30,520
There's a muscle hiding under your biceps.

50
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:32,520
It's called the brachialis.

51
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:34,670
Most people have never even heard of it.

52
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:40,470
But when it grows, it pushes your biceps
up, and makes your whole arm look wider.

53
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:42,750
To train it, do hammer curls.

54
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:46,990
Hold the dumbbells with your palms facing
each other, like you're holding a hammer.

55
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:49,360
Curl them up, and lower them slowly.

56
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:54,130
At home, you can do the same thing with
two backpacks, or two water jugs.

57
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:59,570
Add two or three sets of hammer curls, and
your arms will look thicker from every
angle.

58
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:02,910
Now, three mistakes that keep your arms
small.

59
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,290
Mistake number one.

60
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,650
Swinging the weight.

61
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,680
If your whole body moves, your arms are
not doing the work.

62
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:13,040
Use a lighter weight, and control every
rep.

63
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:14,470
Mistake number two.

64
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,500
Half reps.

65
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:18,580
The stretch at the bottom is where the
growth happens.

66
00:03:18,730 --> 00:03:21,060
If you skip it, you skip the results.

67
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,530
Mistake number three.

68
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:25,140
Training arms every single day.

69
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:27,610
Your muscles don't grow during the
workout.

70
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,470
They grow when you rest.

71
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,680
Two or three times a week is enough.

72
00:03:31,830 --> 00:03:32,880
So here's your plan.

73
00:03:33,030 --> 00:03:34,570
Two or three times a week.

74
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,130
Three sets of each exercise, plus the
hammer curls.

75
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,630
Eight to twelve reps.

76
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:42,930
Take three seconds to lower the weight on
every rep.

77
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:46,440
And try to add one rep, or a little
weight, every week.

78
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:48,640
So what happens after thirty days?

79
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:53,810
In the first two weeks, your arms will
feel stronger, and the pump will be crazy.

80
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:57,010
By day thirty, your sleeves start to feel
tighter.

81
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:02,270
And after a few months of doing this
consistently, your arms will look
completely different.

82
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:06,130
No magic. Just the right exercises, in the
right position.

83
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,850
Your arms are only one part of the
picture.

84
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,610
If you want to know why some skinny guys
are stronger than big guys, watch this
video next.

85
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:18,580
It will change the way you train every
muscle, not just your arms.

86
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:21,460
And if you want more videos like this,
subscribe.

87
00:04:21,610 --> 00:04:24,270
New videos every Tuesday and Saturday.
